WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.890
There are so many new beauty releases

00:00:01.890 --> 00:00:02.970
happening all the time,

00:00:02.970 --> 00:00:04.095
so we gathered some of the

00:00:04.095 --> 00:00:05.820
most-hyped products from August

00:00:05.820 --> 00:00:07.200
to test for ourselves.

00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:09.630
I've been seeing these
gorgeous holo glosses

00:00:09.630 --> 00:00:11.850
from Queen Cosmetics all over TikTok.

00:00:11.850 --> 00:00:14.010
Of course, I had to get three of them.

00:00:14.010 --> 00:00:16.560
These glosses are just
as beautiful in person.

00:00:16.560 --> 00:00:18.330
They honestly feel fine on the lips,

00:00:18.330 --> 00:00:20.400
as long as you don't apply too much.

00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:22.050
I packed on this Electric shade,

00:00:22.050 --> 00:00:23.970
and it did feel a little gritty,

00:00:23.970 --> 00:00:26.820
so I recommend only doing
one to two thin layers

00:00:26.820 --> 00:00:30.090
to avoid that, but these are so cool.

00:00:30.090 --> 00:00:31.190
They look good on their own

00:00:31.190 --> 00:00:32.990
but even better over lipstick,

00:00:32.990 --> 00:00:34.860
especially darker colors.

00:00:34.860 --> 00:00:37.380
This is the new Fenty Beauty Eaze Drop'Lit

00:00:37.380 --> 00:00:39.000
All-Over Glow Enhancer.

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:41.880
It can be worn on its own
to reduce the look of pores

00:00:41.880 --> 00:00:44.730
or mixed into foundation
for some added glow.

00:00:44.730 --> 00:00:45.938
Using this on its own,

00:00:45.938 --> 00:00:48.054
I honestly wasn't very impressed.

00:00:48.054 --> 00:00:50.520
I don't think my pores
were necessarily blurred,

00:00:50.520 --> 00:00:53.400
and I felt like my skin
didn't look that glowy.

00:00:53.400 --> 00:00:56.280
It kind of just looked
like I applied moisturizer.

00:00:56.280 --> 00:00:58.890
I think this worked better
when mixed into a foundation.

00:00:58.890 --> 00:01:01.290
I mixed it with my Eaze
Drop Blurring Skin Tint,

00:01:01.290 --> 00:01:03.570
which I love, and I
noticed it gave my skin

00:01:03.570 --> 00:01:04.860
a nice little glow.

00:01:04.860 --> 00:01:06.900
This skin tint is more on the matte side,

00:01:06.900 --> 00:01:09.480
so I do like that the glow
enhancer made it more dewy.

00:01:09.480 --> 00:01:11.610
However, I don't think
it's such a big difference

00:01:11.610 --> 00:01:14.160
that I can justify buying this product.

00:01:14.160 --> 00:01:15.990
It kind of just feels like an extra step

00:01:15.990 --> 00:01:17.340
that doesn't add much.

00:01:17.340 --> 00:01:20.130
Item Beauty is Addison Rae's beauty brand.

00:01:20.130 --> 00:01:21.870
People rave about its lip oils,

00:01:21.870 --> 00:01:23.160
so I figured I'd test it out

00:01:23.160 --> 00:01:25.290
with a couple of other products too.

00:01:25.290 --> 00:01:27.930
So, this is the Lip Quip
moisturizing lip oil.

00:01:27.930 --> 00:01:30.870
Let me start out by
saying it smells amazing,

00:01:30.870 --> 00:01:32.190
kind of peachy.

00:01:32.190 --> 00:01:34.170
The color was actually
a little more pigmented

00:01:34.170 --> 00:01:35.700
than I expected for a lip oil,

00:01:35.700 --> 00:01:37.800
but I thought it was so pretty.

00:01:37.800 --> 00:01:39.720
The formula is on the thicker side.

00:01:39.720 --> 00:01:41.220
It feels super nourishing

00:01:41.220 --> 00:01:43.320
and just makes your lips look so juicy,

00:01:43.320 --> 00:01:45.210
so I am really into this.

00:01:45.210 --> 00:01:46.890
This is going in my bag.

00:01:46.890 --> 00:01:49.740
Next I tried the Boost
Juice dual-ended lash primer

00:01:49.740 --> 00:01:50.880
and colored mascara.

00:01:50.880 --> 00:01:53.910
So you can use this as a lash
primer or colored mascara.

00:01:53.910 --> 00:01:55.380
The lilac side is for volume,

00:01:55.380 --> 00:01:57.300
and the blue side is for lengthening.

00:01:57.300 --> 00:02:00.000
I have to admit I much
preferred the blue side

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:01.950
as just a colored mascara.

00:02:01.950 --> 00:02:04.890
I feel like once I applied
regular mascara on top of it,

00:02:04.890 --> 00:02:07.260
my lashes just kind of lumped together.

00:02:07.260 --> 00:02:09.600
The lilac side barely
showed up on my lashes,

00:02:09.600 --> 00:02:12.090
but it worked much
better as a lash primer.

00:02:12.090 --> 00:02:14.580
I also tried the Blushin Like cream blush.

00:02:14.580 --> 00:02:16.710
It's supposed to be a
cream-to-powder formula,

00:02:16.710 --> 00:02:18.600
but it just kind of feels like a powder.

00:02:18.600 --> 00:02:20.580
I used my sponge to apply it at first,

00:02:20.580 --> 00:02:22.770
but it just kind of
looked a little splotchy.

00:02:22.770 --> 00:02:24.750
It worked much better with a brush.

00:02:24.750 --> 00:02:26.216
You can also apply it to the lips,

00:02:26.216 --> 00:02:27.424
and it was honestly cute.

00:02:27.424 --> 00:02:28.980
It's buildable, which I like,

00:02:28.980 --> 00:02:31.170
but I don't feel like
this is anything special.

00:02:31.170 --> 00:02:33.540
ColourPop drops new stuff,
like, every other day,

00:02:33.540 --> 00:02:35.970
but these Graphix ink
liners caught my eye.

00:02:35.970 --> 00:02:39.690
I really like this tip. I's
supersharp and flexible.

00:02:39.690 --> 00:02:42.420
I am horrible at doing any
kind of liner situation,

00:02:42.420 --> 00:02:43.470
so I was really glad

00:02:43.470 --> 00:02:45.930
that this tip kind of did the work for me.

00:02:45.930 --> 00:02:50.100
However, the color payoff
on these is not great.

00:02:50.100 --> 00:02:51.990
I found myself layering up the product

00:02:51.990 --> 00:02:54.330
for full color payoff,
and with this formula,

00:02:54.330 --> 00:02:57.450
the more you layer, the
more textured it looks.

00:02:57.450 --> 00:02:59.070
It sucks because these are colors

00:02:59.070 --> 00:03:01.380
that I don't really see
a lot of in eyeliner,

00:03:01.380 --> 00:03:03.930
but this formula is just not my favorite.

00:03:03.930 --> 00:03:05.550
IT Cosmetics just dropped another

00:03:05.550 --> 00:03:07.110
Love is the Foundation brush.

00:03:07.110 --> 00:03:09.450
I think it drops one of these a year.

00:03:09.450 --> 00:03:11.970
I have one from a previous
year that I really love,

00:03:11.970 --> 00:03:13.800
but they're actually not the same.

00:03:13.800 --> 00:03:15.450
This new one is less dense

00:03:15.450 --> 00:03:17.100
and more flexible than my old one,

00:03:17.100 --> 00:03:18.681
and I also feel like the bristles

00:03:18.681 --> 00:03:20.460
on this new one are longer.

00:03:20.460 --> 00:03:22.118
I used it to apply my foundation,

00:03:22.118 --> 00:03:23.826
and I was really happy with how fast

00:03:23.826 --> 00:03:26.882
it blended everything in
without looking streaky.

00:03:26.882 --> 00:03:28.890
It also worked great with my concealer.

00:03:28.890 --> 00:03:30.750
I didn't lose any coverage with this brush

00:03:30.750 --> 00:03:32.460
because it didn't absorb the product.

00:03:32.460 --> 00:03:34.080
I think I actually like this new one

00:03:34.080 --> 00:03:35.610
better than my old one.

00:03:35.610 --> 00:03:37.980
I tried a couple of
products from J.Cat Beauty.

00:03:37.980 --> 00:03:40.050
Let's talk about this blush first.

00:03:40.050 --> 00:03:41.790
This color is so pretty.

00:03:41.790 --> 00:03:43.050
It's like an orangey pink

00:03:43.050 --> 00:03:44.580
with a bunch of gold shimmer in it,

00:03:44.580 --> 00:03:46.605
so you get this very buildable color

00:03:46.605 --> 00:03:48.130
with some added glow.

00:03:48.130 --> 00:03:50.040
I can definitely see this color working

00:03:50.040 --> 00:03:52.230
for so many different skin tones.

00:03:52.230 --> 00:03:54.300
The Mood Flick holo-sparkle lip balm

00:03:54.300 --> 00:03:56.760
is one of those
color-changing lip products.

00:03:56.760 --> 00:03:58.740
I honestly thought these
would be more glittery,

00:03:58.740 --> 00:04:00.900
but I think it just looked metallic on me.

00:04:00.900 --> 00:04:03.720
They do actually feel pretty
moisturizing on the lips.

00:04:03.720 --> 00:04:06.330
I was really surprised
at how much these stain.

00:04:06.330 --> 00:04:07.830
When I was trying to take it off,

00:04:07.830 --> 00:04:09.390
my lips were bright pink.

00:04:09.390 --> 00:04:11.056
I don't know if I'd ever use these again,

00:04:11.056 --> 00:04:11.956
but they're cute.

00:04:11.956 --> 00:04:15.210
I haven't reviewed a Too
Faced product in forever,

00:04:15.210 --> 00:04:16.385
but it just released this

00:04:16.385 --> 00:04:19.578
Born This Way Ethereal
Light smoothing concealer,

00:04:19.578 --> 00:04:21.630
and I heard really good things about it.

00:04:21.630 --> 00:04:24.510
It's supposed to be super
hydrating and smoothing.

00:04:24.510 --> 00:04:26.580
I did not like the applicator on this,

00:04:26.580 --> 00:04:27.570
not because of the shape,

00:04:27.570 --> 00:04:29.970
but because it doesn't
pick up product that well.

00:04:29.970 --> 00:04:32.070
This formula is actually really nice.

00:04:32.070 --> 00:04:34.500
Even after blending it out
and setting it with powder,

00:04:34.500 --> 00:04:37.560
you can still see that
luminosity in the concealer.

00:04:37.560 --> 00:04:39.060
I don't know if it did much smoothing,

00:04:39.060 --> 00:04:40.440
but I like the coverage it gave me

00:04:40.440 --> 00:04:42.270
and how easy it was to work with.

00:04:42.270 --> 00:04:44.820
This is the Dior Rouge Dior Forever

00:04:44.820 --> 00:04:46.503
transfer-proof lipstick.

00:04:46.503 --> 00:04:49.380
Not a liquid lipstick, a regular lipstick.

00:04:49.380 --> 00:04:51.750
So you apply this like any other lipstick,

00:04:51.750 --> 00:04:53.730
wait three minutes for the color to set,

00:04:53.730 --> 00:04:54.750
and you should be left

00:04:54.750 --> 00:04:57.030
with a long-wearing, transfer-proof lip.

00:04:57.030 --> 00:04:59.460
I think this particular
shade was a bit patchy,

00:04:59.460 --> 00:05:01.710
but I evened it out as much as I could.

00:05:01.710 --> 00:05:03.840
I could not believe how well this worked.

00:05:03.840 --> 00:05:05.760
I was expecting a lot of transfer

00:05:05.760 --> 00:05:07.770
because this is a regular lipstick,

00:05:07.770 --> 00:05:09.780
but the transfer was pretty minimal.

00:05:09.780 --> 00:05:12.480
It also didn't feel
too drying on the lips.

00:05:12.480 --> 00:05:14.370
I think this formula is really cool,

00:05:14.370 --> 00:05:15.887
and I want to try out some other shades.

